> 
> Wednesday 6 June 2007
> 
> Time:
> 12:00-1:00 PM US Pacific time
> 1:00-2:00 PM US Mountain time
> 3:00-4:00 PM US Eastern time
> 8:00-9:00 PM Western European time
> 
> FC Backup Number: 712-580-0600
> Conference Code: 839473#
> 
> Our agenda topics should include a continuing discussion of
> Glen's fine proposal for an Embedded Client Thin Thread, in
> particular as a proving ground for additional (not replacement)
> API functions in the various OP modules for naming convergence
> based on the JTAPI/1.0 objects, attributes, and attribute values.
> 
> NOTE:  The following week (Wednesday 13 June 2007), many
> of us will be at the Linux Foundation Summit in Mountain View.
> 
> Claudia - maybe we should just shift our bi-weekly schedule
> permanently?  Just a thought.  What do you think?
> 
> Cheers,
